        {
          "kind": "class",
          "description": "Multiselect control. Form-associated: `name` submits one entry per selected value, a form reset restores the value from connection, and a disabled fieldset disables the control. `value` is the selected values, in selection order. The attribute is a JSON array. A value with no matching option still shows a chip, labeled with the value until an option provides text. Copies `<option>` and `<optgroup>` elements from the `options` slot into the list. Empty-value options are ignored. Disabled options are shown and cannot be toggled. Group labels are headings. Choosing a row toggles that value and leaves the list open. A chip remove drops that value and does not toggle the list. Dispatches `input` and `change` on this host after `value` updates. Both bubble and are composed. Escape, focus leaving the control, and a pointer outside close the list. No public methods. `ui-form-field` writes `description`, `described-by`, `invalid`, and `required`.",
